{"parentUuid":"28e914e6-9f50-43b3-a75d-671c335967cc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BBvKojVbA5BLiQCWYGFwLz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XTuDV5eK94AWfuwfuD1RLB","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools CP-SAT profile propagator hotspot performance"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8118,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8118,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotiknngnrU8qKZ2tFCR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c32d906a-afc4-4504-9d09-175d486c746f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:41.921Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c32d906a-afc4-4504-9d09-175d486c746f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTuDV5eK94AWfuwfuD1RLB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT profile propagator hotspot performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"custom propagator needed ? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3303\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3303\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/ortools/sat\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"📈 #76 Optimizing with Google OR-Tools: strategies and insights from three years of real-world experience\",\"url\":\"https://www.feasible.club/p/76-optimizing-with-google-or-tools\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant resources about OR-Tools CP-SAT and its propagation mechanisms:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Propagation in CP-SAT:**\n\nPropagation shrinks variable domains by local reasoning (all-different, cumulative, bounds), and every propagator can explain why it shrank a domain with that explanation pushed into the SAT core as a clause.\n\n**Propagation Performance Considerations:**\n\nIn packing problems, certain expensive propagation techniques can significantly speed up the search but can also drastically slow it down if misused. Compressing table constraints leads to less Booleans and faster propagation but can reduce the quality of the LP relaxation.\n\n**CP-SAT Architecture:**\n\nCP-SAT marries constraint programming (propagation) with SAT solving (learned clauses) and sprinkles in cutting-plane tricks. CP-SAT includes propagation algorithms for classic CP constraints (XOR, circuit, non-overlapping rectangles), disjunctive scheduling constraints, and cumulative scheduling constraints.\n\n**Profile and Hotspot Analysis:**\n\nThe search results do not contain specific information about profiling tools or hotspot performance analysis for the CP-SAT propagator. For detailed performance profiling information, you may want to consult the [OR-Tools GitHub repository](https://github.com/google/or-tools) directly or the official OR-Tools documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"10d2abea-c329-43f7-880e-23d05ba736e2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:49.024Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c32d906a-afc4-4504-9d09-175d486c746f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"28e914e6-9f50-43b3-a75d-671c335967cc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PH8441Sh1xS6S1h7HGddmm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"py-spy native flag profile C++ extension Python 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Profiling Native Python Extensions - Ben Frederickson\",\"url\":\"https://www.benfrederickson.com/profiling-native-python-extensions-with-py-spy/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - benfred/py-spy: Sampling profiler for Python programs · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/benfred/py-spy\"},{\"title\":\"py-spy: Sampling Profiler for Python | pydevtools\",\"url\":\"https://pydevtools.com/handbook/reference/py-spy/\"},{\"title\":\"Profile Native Extensions · Issue #2 · benfred/py-spy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/benfred/py-spy/issues/2\"},{\"title\":\"How to Profile Python Applications with cProfile and py-spy\",\"url\":\"https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2025-01-06-profile-python-cprofile-pyspy/view\"},{\"title\":\"py-spy - Sampling Profiler for Python Code by Sunny Solanki\",\"url\":\"https://coderzcolumn.com/tutorials/python/py-spy-sampling-profiler-for-python-code\"},{\"title\":\"py-spy – Low‑overhead Sampling Profiler for Python | PickYourTech\",\"url\":\"https://www.pickyourtech.com/projects/gh-benfred-py-spy\"},{\"title\":\"Python Performance Profiling Using PySpy — Squirro Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.squirro.com/en/latest/technical/admin/troubleshooting/python-profiling-pyspy.html\"},{\"title\":\"Python Slow, Can't Change Code? py-spy Zero-Intrusion Sampling, Live Flame Graphs | via X-CMD | py-spy\",\"url\":\"https://www.x-cmd.com/install/py-spy/\"},{\"title\":\"py-spy 0.1.4 - Docs.rs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/crate/py-spy/0.1.4\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about py-spy's native flag for profiling C++ extensions in Python:\n\n## py-spy Native Flag Overview\n\nWith the 0.2 release of py-spy, if you enable native extension profiling with the --native flag you will get a profile containing both python code and C++/Cython code.\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe --native flag captures C, C++, and Cython frames alongside Python frames. For best results, you should compile your Python extension with symbols.\n\n## Platform Support\n\nNative support covers Linux (x86_64, ARM, 32-bit ARM) and Windows (x86_64); the project does not claim native support on macOS.\n\n## Technical Implementation\n\nAll that is needed to profile native extensions is to get the native call stack and then merge in the python callstack. We already have code from the first version of py-spy to get the python stack, so the first challenge here is getting the native stack to merge in. To get the native stack I used the StackWalk64 API on Windows and used libunwind-ptrace on Linux.\n\n## Recent Updates\n\nThe project is actively maintained but has long gaps between releases; v0.4.1 (July 2025) followed v0.4.0 (November 2024), which itself followed v0.3.14 (September 2022).\n\nThe --native flag is particularly useful for profiling performance-critical libraries like NumPy and Pandas that use C/C++ extensions underneath their Python interfaces.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8a767fe9-cef5-47c1-a38f-18531a406441","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:08:49.052Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"28e914e6-9f50-43b3-a75d-671c335967cc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
