{"parentUuid":"8343398e-2a19-4664-911f-84220681dfde","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9ZGxTdKTpcLwLqPpvf7cS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT no_overlap_2d propagator cumulative performance bottleneck\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter documentation NoOverlap2D, Cumulative · google/or-tools · Discussion #3107\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3107\"},{\"title\":\"Performance of packing problems · google/or-tools · Discussion #3177\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3177\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"custom propagator needed ? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3303\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3303\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the CP-SAT `no_overlap_2d` propagator and its performance characteristics:\n\nThe `no_overlap_2d` propagator is acknowledged as having poor performance, with developers noting the lack of time to implement stronger versions.\n\nRecent improvements have been made, including new parameters such as `use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d` and the renaming of `use_cumulative_in_no_overlap_2d` to `use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d`.\n\nRegarding the relationship between the propagators and cumulative constraints, the improvements to NoOverlap2D constraints come from improving propagations from already present cumulative constraints, or by automatically deducing cumulative constraints from NoOverlap2D constraints.\n\nThe search results indicate that enhancing the `no_overlap_2d` propagator through better integration with cumulative constraint propagation strategies has been an area of active development in CP-SAT, particularly focusing on techniques like energetic reasoning and timetabling to address performance bottlenecks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dcea1916-378f-4369-a5c4-440bce54219e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:10.673Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8343398e-2a19-4664-911f-84220681dfde","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d05d6691-55b7-4271-9fa1-46603f71a99b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018wqvkiMiGqkzF3wzeVNhjb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Windows Performance Analyzer WPA ETW C++ profiling tutorial PerfView\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Tutorial: vcperf and Windows Performance Analyzer | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build-insights/tutorials/vcperf-and-wpa?view=msvc-170\"},{\"title\":\"Windows Performance Analyzer: Complete WPA Guide\",\"url\":\"https://trainsec.net/library/windows-internals/introduction-to-the-windows-performance-analyzer/\"},{\"title\":\"Windows Performance Analyzer | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/test/wpt/windows-performance-analyzer\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - microsoft/perfview: PerfView is a CPU and memory performance-analysis tool · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/microsoft/perfview\"},{\"title\":\"Windows Performance Analyzer: How to use tutorial, Download, Install\",\"url\":\"https://www.thewindowsclub.com/windows-performance-analyzer\"},{\"title\":\"Tutorial: Windows Performance Analyzer basics | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build-insights/tutorials/wpa-basics?view=msvc-170\"},{\"title\":\"Windows Performance Analyzer (WPA) plugin | Arm Learning Paths\",\"url\":\"https://learn.arm.com/install-guides/windows-perf-wpa-plugin/\"},{\"title\":\"Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) | wtrace.net\",\"url\":\"https://wtrace.net/guides/etw/\"},{\"title\":\"Windows Performance Analyzer step-by-step guide | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/test/wpt/wpa-step-by-step-guide\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started Windows Performance Analyzer | Microsoft Learn\",\"url\":\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/test/wpt/getting-started--windows-performance-analyzer--wpa-\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about Windows Performance Analyzer, ETW profiling, and related tools. Here's a summary of the search results:\n\n## Key Resources Found:\n\n**Windows Performance Analyzer (WPA) Overview:**\nWPA is included in the Windows Assessment and Deployment Kit (Windows ADK) and creates graphs and data tables of Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) events that are recorded by Windows Performance Recorder (WPR), Xperf, or an assessment that is run in the Assessment Platform.\n\n**C++ Build Insights Profiling:**\nThere's a tutorial on how to use vcperf and WPA for analyzing C++ build traces. WPA is a trace viewer available in the Windows Assessment and Deployment Kit (ADK) and is a separate utility that's not part of the components you can install with the Visual Studio installer.\n\n**PerfView Tool:**\nPerfView is a free performance-analysis tool that helps isolate CPU and memory-related performance issues and works for a wide variety of scenarios, but has a number of special features for investigating performance issues in code written for the .NET runtime. PerfView is built on a library called Microsoft.Diagnostics.Tracing.TraceEvent, that knows how to both collect and parse Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) and EventPipe (.NET Core trace) data.\n\n**Getting Started:**\nYou can download and install the latest version of the Windows ADK, and when prompted for the features you want to install, select the Windows Performance Toolkit.\n\nThe search results include Microsoft Learn tutorials, GitHub repositories, and comprehensive guides for using these profiling tools together.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"25618585-8c35-4578-b7f4-3cc73817c148","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:12.027Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d05d6691-55b7-4271-9fa1-46603f71a99b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"db194f0f-72a4-4a87-a298-bb6fcb800961","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QsWWvrqGtQhH6mdMc8G4fM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"scalene austin python profiler comparison 2025 cpu memory native\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - plasma-umass/scalene: Scalene: a high-performance, high-precision CPU, GPU, and memory profiler for Python with AI-powered optimization proposals · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/plasma-umass/scalene\"},{\"title\":\"scalene · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/scalene/0.9.15/\"},{\"title\":\"Triangulating Python Performance Issues with Scalene\",\"url\":\"https://www.usenix.org/system/files/osdi23-berger.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Triangulating Python Performance Issues with SCALENE | USENIX\",\"url\":\"https://www.usenix.org/conference/osdi23/presentation/berger\"},{\"title\":\"scalene - A high-performance, high-precision CPU, GPU, and memory profiler for Python with AI-powered optimization proposals\",\"url\":\"https://libs.tech/project/228700143/scalene\"},{\"title\":\"Profiler Powered by Scalene: AI-Powered Python Profiling in Cursor | WaYdotNET --> WEB AND DEVOPS\",\"url\":\"https://www.waydotnet.com/posts/profiler-powered-by-scalene-extension/\"},{\"title\":\"Scalene - A Python Profiler Case Study\",\"url\":\"https://anandksub.dev/blog/scalene-profiling\"},{\"title\":\"Profiling Scalene Py-Spy: Memory CPU Flamegraphs 2025\",\"url\":\"https://johal.in/profiling-scalene-py-spy-memory-cpu-flamegraphs-2025/\"},{\"title\":\"Open-Source AI-Powered Optimization in Scalene: Advancing Python Performance Profiling with DeepSeek-R1 and LLaMA 3.2\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2502.10299\"},{\"title\":\"Scalene - CPU and Memory Profiler for Python Code by Sunny Solanki\",\"url\":\"https://coderzcolumn.com/tutorials/python/scalene-cpu-and-memory-profiler-for-python-code\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Scalene, Austin, and Python profiler comparisons for 2025:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Scalene's Performance:**\nScalene's overhead is just a 35% slowdown, and its overhead is typically no more than 10-20% (and often less).\n\n**Scalene vs. Austin Comparison:**\nWhile Austin is faster, as Section 6.3 shows, it provides inaccurate estimates of memory consumption. This comes from a USENIX research paper on Scalene's performance.\n\n**CPU and Memory Profiling:**\nScalene separates out time spent in Python from time in native code (including libraries). Key Scalene-only features include: Python vs. C time breakdown, system time separation, memory trends reporting, GPU profiling, copy volume reporting, and automatic leak detection.\n\n**2025 Updates:**\nScalene's 3-way profiling (CPU/Python/CUDA) outperforms traditional tools by attributing time accurately to Python lines, reducing false positives by 50%. Additionally, Scalene was extended to provide AI-powered optimization suggestions using open-source language models like DeepSeek-R1 and LLaMA 3.2.\n\n**Recent Version:**\nScalene version 1.5.51 was released on 2025.01.29.\n\nThe search results indicate that Scalene offers more accurate memory profiling compared to Austin, though Austin has slightly lower overhead for CPU profiling.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7a3cc7b3-0683-4ead-8c4e-4a1535b95fe1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:12.108Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"db194f0f-72a4-4a87-a298-bb6fcb800961","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7a3cc7b3-0683-4ead-8c4e-4a1535b95fe1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WeVCjPGZ5mFhRtdc6eoosv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ZpCAzQ2pGiEoa1i2eFMxg","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.benfrederickson.com/profiling-native-python-extensions-with-py-spy/","prompt":"Extract concrete commands and platform support for py-spy --native flag on Windows and Linux. Include exact py-spy record / py-spy top command syntax and any prerequisites about debug symbols."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1522,"cache_read_input_tokens":27859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1522,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotmGVXQgemrmC2tTSjh","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3fe350d-9568-4058-9e5b-7a09924b7222","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:15.922Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c3fe350d-9568-4058-9e5b-7a09924b7222","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WeVCjPGZ5mFhRtdc6eoosv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QKsd9s2wcjdu3Jhpg3ZBQh","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html","prompt":"Extract the key sections of CP-SAT log to look at when performance is poor. Specifically: which fields show propagator time, which show LP time, which show subsolver time. Include the parameter names like log_subsolver_statistics. Quote any concrete log field names."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1522,"cache_read_input_tokens":27859,"output_tokens":360,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1522},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2612,"output_tokens":360,"cache_read_input_tokens":27859,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1522,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotmGVXQgemrmC2tTSjh","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f1a9105-b9d5-48c5-875e-0a9f3e6a6d0a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:18.204Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c3fe350d-9568-4058-9e5b-7a09924b7222","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ZpCAzQ2pGiEoa1i2eFMxg","type":"tool_result","content":"# py-spy Native Extension Profiling Commands\n\n## Platform Support\n\nThe article explicitly states this feature works on **x86_64 Linux and Windows only**. OSX, FreeBSD, and ARM/i686 Linux are not yet supported.\n\n## Command Syntax\n\nThe article mentions enabling native profiling with \"the `--native` flag\" but does not provide the exact command syntax for `py-spy record` or `py-spy top` with concrete examples.\n\n## Key Prerequisites\n\nFor effective native extension profiling:\n\n1. **Debug Symbols Required**: \"For best results you should compile your extension with symbols, you may see pointer addresses if we fail to symbolicate.\"\n\n2. **Cython Compilation Option**: Use `emit_linenums=True` during cythonize calls, as this enables proper line mapping back to original .pyx files.\n\n3. **Development Installation**: If `emit_linenums=True` isn't used, \"the generated C file isn't installed with the extension, so this usually only works if you are running a development version (`python setup.py develop` or `pip install -e .`)\"\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe article notes this \"adds some extra processing time - especially on Windows\" and doesn't yet support Docker containers profiled from the host OS."}]},"uuid":"40169e5c-56bd-4958-9113-b9d5ed7416b0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:20.483Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c3fe350d-9568-4058-9e5b-7a09924b7222","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7f1a9105-b9d5-48c5-875e-0a9f3e6a6d0a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QKsd9s2wcjdu3Jhpg3ZBQh","type":"tool_result","content":"# Key CP-SAT Log Sections for Performance Analysis\n\nBased on the primer, here are the critical log areas to examine when performance is poor:\n\n## Search Phase Log\nThe most important section is **\"The search progress log is an essential element of the overall log, crucial for identifying performance bottlenecks.\"** This shows how bounds improve over time and which subsolvers contribute solutions.\n\n## Subsolver Details Section\nThis contains detailed timing information. Look for:\n- **Task timing table** - Shows duration for each subsolver (e.g., `'core'`, `'default_lp'`, `'lb_tree_search'`)\n- Individual subsolver execution counts and average runtimes\n- LP-related timing within `'default_lp'` entries\n\n## Key Fields to Monitor\n\nThe summary mentions these performance indicators:\n- **`lp_iterations`** - Linear programming work\n- **`propagations`** and **`integer_propagations`** - Constraint propagation activity\n- **`deterministic_time`** - Standardized timing metric\n- **`gap_integral`** - \"A lower value will indicate that the solver is converging faster\"\n\n## Parameter Configuration\n\nTo enable detailed logging, use:\n```\nsolver.parameters.log_search_progress = True\n```\n\nThe primer notes that subsolver-level analysis requires deep expertise, and the **Log Analyzer tool** is recommended for visualization rather than manual inspection of raw timing data."}]},"uuid":"1a209cb5-e8c0-4f1e-bdde-54f017d0ec34","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:24.210Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7f1a9105-b9d5-48c5-875e-0a9f3e6a6d0a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
