{"parentUuid":"334a3e2e-0378-4101-b6bd-b7632d341d32","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JzaLJHH3XK5cesKmbSd3aM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AU5nrT8TjS6hVJsPUaDv4u","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"VTune hotspot analysis attach PID Python ortools real world"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3820,"cache_read_input_tokens":33288,"output_tokens":156,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3820},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":156,"cache_read_input_tokens":33288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3820,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoto1Qik7cBwVnvKFvo2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"48719906-c8b0-4686-bcda-0e77c7b80871","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:42.677Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"334a3e2e-0378-4101-b6bd-b7632d341d32","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NQc9m7XJnerm82REpTgaC3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" cp_sat \"deterministic_time\" propagation count log fields\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"Deterministic execution time for CP Sat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/ZGj5vhhZX48\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the OR-Tools CP-SAT solver and its logging fields, particularly regarding `deterministic_time` and propagation count.\n\nIn the CP-SAT solver response log, key fields include: propagations (the number of propagation steps), integer_propagations, and deterministic_time (a measure of solver work independent of wall-clock time).\n\nThe `deterministic_time` field represents a clock-independent measure of solver execution, while `walltime` shows the actual elapsed time in seconds. A lower deterministic_time value combined with the gap_integral field can indicate that the solver is converging faster.\n\nThe search results also show examples of how propagation counts are logged. In the presolve phase, CP-SAT logs entries like \"[Probing] deterministic_time: 1.00049 (limit: 1)\" along with work metrics and the number of fixes applied during boolean propagation.\n\nThese fields are part of the standard `CpSolverResponse` summary that CP-SAT produces when logging search progress is enabled, helping users understand the solver's behavior and performance characteristics.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0cd1a409-ddce-4b21-b874-cdfe50fd100e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:44.679Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"334a3e2e-0378-4101-b6bd-b7632d341d32","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"48719906-c8b0-4686-bcda-0e77c7b80871","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"263c4537-7eaf-4141-8243-2bd92971b2f2","agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AU5nrT8TjS6hVJsPUaDv4u","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VTune hotspot analysis attach PID Python ortools real world\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Python* Code Analysis\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/vtune-profiler/user-guide/2024-0/python-code-analysis.html\"},{\"title\":\"Finding Hotspots in Your Code with the Intel VTune Command-Line Interface - HECC Knowledge Base\",\"url\":\"https://www.nas.nasa.gov/hecc/support/kb/finding-hotspots-in-your-code-with-the-intel-vtune-command-line-interface_506.html\"},{\"title\":\"Python* Code Analysis\",\"url\":\"http://portal.nacad.ufrj.br/online/intel/vtune2017/help/GUID-069D2886-7357-4729-8785-88B43B1292E2.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to Track Multiple Processes by PID in VTune Profiler - Intel Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.intel.com/t5/Analyzers/How-to-Track-Multiple-Processes-by-PID-in-VTune-Profiler/td-p/1555871\"},{\"title\":\"Intel VTune profiler — Scipion 3.0.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://scipion-em.github.io/docs/release-3.0.0/docs/developer/vtune-profiler.html\"},{\"title\":\"target-pid\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/vtune-profiler/user-guide/2023-0/target-pid.html\"},{\"title\":\"vTune results - Intel Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.intel.com/t5/Analyzers/vTune-results/m-p/1350340\"},{\"title\":\"Hotspots Analysis for CPU Usage Issues\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/vtune-profiler/user-guide/2024-0/basic-hotspots-analysis.html\"},{\"title\":\"Profiling Machine Learning Applications (NEW)\",\"url\":\"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/vtune-profiler/cookbook/2023-1/profiling-machine-learning-applications.html\"},{\"title\":\"VTune Profiler with Python - No result - Intel Communities\",\"url\":\"https://community.intel.com/t5/Analyzers/VTune-Profiler-with-Python-No-result/td-p/1195072\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I've found relevant information about using VTune hotspot analysis with Python and attaching to processes by PID. Here's what I found:\n\n## VTune Hotspot Analysis with Attach to PID for Python\n\nTo perform hotspot analysis on Python processes, you can select the \"Attach to Process\" target type in VTune, specify the Python process name or PID, and select the Hotspots analysis type.\n\n### Command-Line Usage\n\nYou can use the target-pid option to attach a collect or collect-with action to a running process specified by its process ID (pid). For example, you can attach a hotspots collection to a running process whose ID is 1234.\n\n### Python-Specific Considerations\n\nWhen you attach VTune to the Python process, make sure you initialize the Global Interpreter Lock (GIL) inside your script before you start the analysis. \n\nAdditionally, Intel VTune supports Basic Hotspots and Locks and Waits analysis for Python applications via the Launch Application and Attach to Process modes.\n\n### Python Profiling Best Practices\n\nTo get the maximum performance out of your Python application, consider using native extensions, such as NumPy or writing and compiling performance critical modules of your Python project in native languages, such as C, which will help your application take advantage of vectorization and make complete use of powerful CPU resources.\n\nNote: The search results don't contain specific examples related to OR-Tools, so you may need to apply these general VTune hotspot analysis techniques to profile OR-Tools-based applications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"23b0020f-d836-412a-8812-ff0b9ee9b4a0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:09:52.297Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"48719906-c8b0-4686-bcda-0e77c7b80871","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"23b0020f-d836-412a-8812-ff0b9ee9b4a0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a03cda5a8b71604d1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RJUPR76YHSVSBNn9wMvHwH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me consolidate into the requested compact deliverable.\n\n# CP-SAT Profile/Trace 工具调研报告\n\n## Windows 推荐三件套\n\n| 工具 | 强项 | 适配我们项目 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **py-spy 0.4.1 + `--native`** | 采样式、零侵入、能穿透 Python→C++ 调用栈，输出 SVG flamegraph | 首选。装一行命令，能直接看到 `_propagate_no_overlap_2d` 这种 C++ 函数 |\n| **Intel VTune Profiler 2025.4** | Hardware PMU 级别精度，能看 cache miss / branch miss / TLB miss，免费（oneAPI Base Toolkit） | 第二步深挖。Hotspots + Microarch Exploration 两种 analysis 都可以 attach PID |\n| **Superluminal Performance** (商业, 也可用 PerfView 替代) | 8–40 kHz 采样，无侵入、可视化时间线最干净；PerfView 是微软免费版（基于 ETW） | 长跑 168h 时跑短窗口验证。PerfView 适合不想买 license 的情况 |\n\n> Visual Studio Profiler 也是 ETW-based，但 UI 比 PerfView 更迟钝；WPA 适合看 OS-level 事件（IO、context switch），不适合 propagator-level 追踪。\n\n## Linux 推荐三件套\n\n| 工具 | 强项 | 用法要点 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`perf record -F 999 -g --call-graph=dwarf`** + Brendan Gregg's FlameGraph | 内核级、极低开销、最经典 | `perf script \\| stackcollapse-perf.pl \\| flamegraph.pl > out.svg`。需要 ortools 带 `-g` 编译，否则只能看符号偏移。新版 perf 支持 `perf script report flamegraph` 一行出图 |\n| **py-spy --native (Linux x86_64)** | 比 perf 更易用、不需要 root；用 `libunwind-ptrace` 抓 native stack | `py-spy record -o profile.svg --native --pid <PID> --duration 60` |\n| **`bpftrace` / eBPF** | 自定义事件（比如只统计某个 propagator 调用次数） | 例：`bpftrace -e 'uprobe:libortools.so:NoOverlap2DConstraint::Propagate { @[ustack] = count(); }'` 适合定位单个 propagator |\n\n> Valgrind callgrind 准确但慢 50–100×，不适合 CP-SAT（解一次几十分钟，callgrind 下要几十小时）。Scalene 是 CPU+memory+GPU 三合一 Python 专用，但对 ortools 这种重 C++ 的 native 部分定位不如 py-spy --native。\n\n## 给我们项目的具体操作清单\n\n### 第 0 步：先用 CP-SAT 内置日志（不花一分钱）\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.log_search_progress = True\nsolver.parameters.log_subsolver_statistics = True   # 关键\nsolver.parameters.log_callback = lambda s: log_file.write(s + \"\\n\")\n```\n\n然后用 `pip install cpsat-logutils` 解析，重点看四个字段：\n- `deterministic_time`（与 wall time 对比，看是不是被 GIL/调度拖累）\n- `propagations` / `integer_propagations`（哪个 worker 在空转）\n- 每个 subsolver 的 `task timing`（`default_lp` / `core` / `no_lp` / `lb_tree_search` 谁占大头）\n- `gap_integral`（收敛速度）\n\n如果 `default_lp` 占 >50% → 调 `linearization_level`；若 `no_lp` 占大头 → 是纯 propagation 慢，下面用 profiler 定位。\n\n### 第 1 步：py-spy 60 秒快照（Windows 实操）\n\n```powershell\npip install py-spy\n# 跑 main.py，记下 PID（telemetry 已经有 process_tree_telemetry）\npy-spy record -o D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.profiling\\sat_native.svg `\n    --native --pid <PID> --duration 60 --rate 200\n# 浏览器打开 svg，搜 \"Propagate\" / \"NoOverlap\" / \"LP\" 看占比\n```\n\nortools 官方 wheel 有 PDB，符号能解到 `operations_research::sat::NoOverlap2DConstraint::Propagate`。\n\n### 第 2 步：VTune Hotspots（深挖，需要 30 分钟跑完）\n\n```powershell\n# 安装：oneAPI Base Toolkit Online Installer 2025.4\nvtune -collect hotspots -target-pid <PID> -duration 120 `\n      -result-dir D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.profiling\\vtune_r001\nvtune-gui D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.profiling\\vtune_r001\n```\n\n切到 **Microarchitecture Exploration** analysis 看 Backend Bound（cache miss）vs Bad Speculation（branch miss）。如果 Backend > 40% → 模型太大撑爆 L2/L3；考虑减少 binding 变量数。\n\n### 第 3 步：集成到 telemetry\n\n在 `src/runtime/process_tree_telemetry.py` 加一个 hook：当 wave 检测到某候选 wall_time > 90 percentile 时，自动 spawn `py-spy record --pid <wave_pid> --duration 30 -o outliers/<cand_id>.svg`。这是 D 通道（runtime diagnostics）的天然延伸，且符合 AI 安全契约（只采样，不写 checkpoint）。\n\n## Profile 后预期能找到的热点\n\n基于 70×70 + 266 设施的模型规模，以及社区已知 CP-SAT 性能特性，热点分布大概率是：\n\n1. **`NoOverlap2DConstraint::Propagate`（30–50%）** — 官方承认这个 propagator 弱，且我们 266 个矩形都在用。可以试 `use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d=true` 和 `use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d=true` 各做一次 A/B\n2. **LP simplex / cut generation（20–35%）** — 取决于 `linearization_level`（默认 1）。如果热，降到 0 试试\n3. **`PrecedencesPropagator` + `IntegerTrail::EnqueueLiteral`（10–20%）** — binding/routing 的链式约束自然热\n4. **clause learning / VSIDS heap（5–15%）** — 通常不是瓶颈，除非冲突率特别高\n5. **Python ↔ C++ 边界（<5%）** — proto 序列化，基本可忽略\n\n## 第一步具体计划（今晚就能做）\n\n1. 在现有 `main.py` 加 4 行 `log_subsolver_statistics=True` + log 落盘；跑一个已知慢的候选 30 分钟\n2. `pip install cpsat-logutils py-spy`，先看 log 哪个 subsolver 占大头\n3. 同一个候选再跑一次，开一个 PowerShell 并行执行 `py-spy record --native --pid <PID> --duration 120` 抓 flamegraph\n4. 把 `log_subsolver_statistics` 的 task timing 表 + flamegraph 放在 `.profiling/baseline_<候选id>/` 下作为 baseline\n5. 如果 NoOverlap2D 果然占大头，下一轮做 `use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d` 的 A/B，复用 S6 worker matrix 框架\n\n整个第一步不到 4 小时，零侵入、不动 PROJECT_LOCK 边界，纯诊断信息，符合 AI 安全契约（D 通道 runtime diagnostics）。\n\n## 关键链接\n\n- [py-spy native 介绍 (Ben Frederickson)](https://www.benfrederickson.com/profiling-native-python-extensions-with-py-spy/)\n- [py-spy GitHub](https://github.com/benfred/py-spy)\n- [CP-SAT Primer · Understanding the Log](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html)\n- [cpsat-logutils](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils)\n- [sat_parameters.proto (含 use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [OR-Tools NoOverlap2D 性能讨论 #3107 / packing 性能 #3177](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3177)\n- [Intel VTune for Windows 2025 入门](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/vtune-profiler/get-started-guide/2025-4/windows-os.html)\n- [VTune Python Code Analysis](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/vtune-profiler/user-guide/2025-4/python-code-analysis.html)\n- [Brendan Gregg perf + FlameGraph](https://www.brendangregg.com/perf.html)\n- [FlameGraph repo](https://github.com/brendangregg/FlameGraph)\n- [PerfView (微软免费 ETW 分析器)](https://github.com/microsoft/perfview)\n- [Superluminal C++ 商业采样器](https://superluminal.eu/cplusplus/)\n- [Scalene OSDI'23 论文](https://www.usenix.org/system/files/osdi23-berger.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2659,"cache_read_input_tokens":37108,"output_tokens":3356,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2659},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3356,"cache_read_input_tokens":37108,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2659,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaotpE9UCPgcNVgpSHxhY","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"596fdb20-8435-4afc-b4ee-8cbb752e53b3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:10:51.298Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
